 {"t": "Factory Power Factor Correction", "g": "Electrical", "tier": "compounded",
  "d": "A factory paid power-factor penalties every month: the case covers the correction from audit to capacitor banks. The audit found 0.72 PF from motor loads; the design added switched capacitor stages; the utility verified 0.96.\nResults: penalties eliminated, 11% demand reduction, payback in 14 months.",
  "h": "The case works as a power-quality economics lesson: the audit measured the real reactive load (not the nameplate sum) across the production cycle, sizing the correction to the actual need. The switched stages (not one fixed bank) matched the correction to the varying load - fixed correction overcorrects at light load, causing leading power factor and its own problems. Detuning reactors protected against harmonic resonance: capacitors and system inductance can resonate, amplifying harmonics destructively. The utility verification closed the billing loop - the penalty disappeared from the actual bill. The 11% demand reduction came free with the correction. The lesson: measure first, switch the stages, detune for harmonics.",
  "f": ["Audited the real reactive load across the cycle; sized to reality.",
        "Used switched stages for the varying load; fixed banks overcorrect light.",
        "Added detuning reactors; capacitor resonance amplifies harmonics.",
        "Verified on the utility bill; the penalty's disappearance is the proof.",
        "11% demand reduction came with the correction.",
        "Payback in 14 months from penalties and demand alone."],
  "r": ["Power quality audit: PF across the production cycle.",
        "Capacitor bank design with switching and detuning.",
        "Harmonic assessment for the resonance check.",
        "Utility billing verification."],
  "s": [0, 3, 1], "c": [3, 5, 0],
  "demo": ("case", {"metrics": [("power factor", 0.72, 0.96, "ratio", "up"), ("demand charges", 100.0, 89.0, "% of baseline", "down")]})},
